00:07:02.776 --> 00:07:06.807
<v Host>Time for a short quiz. Listen and try to answer.

00:07:07.408 --> 00:07:13.168
<v Slow>「五山送り火」は、どこで行われましたか。

00:07:13.968 --> 00:07:18.815
<v Host>In Kyoto — big fires were lit on five mountains around the city.

00:07:19.415 --> 00:07:23.759
<v Slow>火は、何時にともりましたか。

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:30.776
<v Host>At eight in the evening. The famous character meaning big was lit first, on the eastern mountain.

00:07:31.375 --> 00:07:36.271
<v Slow>送り火は、何のための火ですか。

00:07:37.072 --> 00:07:44.079
<v Host>They are fires for sending off the spirits of ancestors, who people believe come back home in the middle of August.

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:56.920
<v Host>That's all for today. Once a year, the mountains of Kyoto light up to say goodbye — to the ancestors, and slowly, to summer itself. See you next time on Japanese Daily News.

00:07:57.519 --> 00:07:59.920
<v News>また明日。
